// QA joint scan×enrich rescan-preservation e2e (preserve-enrichment-rescan
// group 4, Tier 1). The FULL production path — real serial-scanner +
// serial-parser + shikimori subprocesses over a real fixture library, the
// qa_serial_e2e_test.go harness patterns — proves the two-tier rescan contract
// end to end:
//
//   - preserved: an UNCHANGED re-scan of a settled (ready) library derives
//     zero ENRICHMENT work — every series and episode document compares
//     byte-equivalent to its pre-rescan snapshot in sources, _provenance,
//     _view, identifiers.shikimori_id, parsed, and ffprobe; _stages is
//     byte-equivalent EXCEPT exactly the truthful skipped entries the enrich
//     queue appends per derive pass for the contractually namespace-less
//     plugin×row shapes (frame-grabber on series rows, shikimori on episode
//     rows) — the AMENDED scenario (specs/scan-library, "Enriched library
//     survives a rescan end-to-end", probe 0149c43a097537b4), asserted here
//     entry-exact, not exempted. Every row still reads ready, and the
//     shikimori stub's recorded request list is UNCHANGED.
//
//   - rederived: a fixture change that alters one episode's parsed identity
//     drops that row's derived namespaces at the re-scan and re-derives them
//     through the real chain, while every untouched row keeps its carried
//     namespaces byte-equivalent and stays ready.
//
//     NOTE on the parsed-identity mechanism: the shipped serial-scanner derives
//     every parsed fact from NAMES (path/extension/sidecar association —
//     plugins/serial-scanner scanner.go parsed()); file BYTES move only the
//     ffprobe base (tier B), which preserves namespaces. So the rederivation
//     leg realizes "the item's parsed identity changes between scans" the only
//     way real disk can: the episode's matched subtitle sidecar is renamed out
//     of its SxxExx match into the serial-level bucket. One rename changes BOTH
//     the episode's parsed.sidecars (1 → 0) AND its series'
//     parsed.series_sidecars (0 → 1) — tier A for both rows — while leaving
//     every identity (library, relative path) intact.
//
// HERMETIC: the shikimori stage is pinned to a local httptest stub through
// MELLIFERA_SHIKIMORI_UPSTREAM (the server subprocess env carries it; the
// plugin child bakes the stub origin into every fetch template) — no test byte
// reaches shikimori.io, and the stub's recorded calls double as the no-network
// proof. All helpers are qaRescan-prefixed to stay collision-free in package
// mellifera_test; the shared harness (buildBinary / qaSerialStartServer /
// qaSerialCreateLibrary / qaSerialWaitSettled / qaSerialMedia / listItems /
// scanLibrary / parseAsyncDoc / deepEqualJSON) is reused as-is.
package itest

